--- MESSAGE ---
A type parameter is a JSON node, on the value-type terms

`TypeName.typeParameters` is a sequence of JSON nodes: a string is the authored text — the whole
corpus today, the header bounds `S <: DomainType` and `T <: Product` included — and a tree will be a
type form once the parser trees the header. TypeName's structural identity compares the nodes as it
compared the strings. Because identity is not rewritten in place, the engine spells each parameter for
Scala at its render sites, through the same target rendering a value type takes; the surface spells a
string verbatim and a tree as any type form.

TypeName's trio moves drake-first, regenerated with the compiled tools. Domain, Rule and Type
re-canonicalize from the drake, closing the three-field residue the type-form commit left. No
definition otherwise moves.

Next: the parser trees the header's parameters and a reference's arguments, and the corpus
re-canonicalizes from the drake.

